# SonoJS registry parity — single source

**Source of truth for UI:** `packages/ui/src/components/…`  
`npm run registry:build` reads that source, rewrites imports to `@/…`, and writes `public/r/`.

| Surface | Path | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Edit here | `packages/ui/src/components/…` | Docs preview + install payload |
| Blocks / charts | `registry/blocks/`, `registry/charts/` | Still authored under `registry/` |
| Built output | `public/r/<item>.json` | What `add` installs — never hand-edit |

Do **not** keep a second hand-edited copy under `registry/ui/`.

## After any UI edit

1. Change `packages/ui/src/components/<name>.tsx` (and examples if needed).
2. Run `npm run registry:build`.
3. Spot-check `public/r/<name>.json`.

```bash
# Edit button → rebuild install payload
# packages/ui/src/components/button.tsx
npm run registry:build
```

## Checklist

- [ ] Only `packages/ui` (or blocks/charts) was edited for UI
- [ ] `npm run registry:build` run after the change
- [ ] Docs preview matches what lands in `public/r/<name>.json`

Human docs: `registry/README.md` · build: `scripts/build-registry.mjs`
